.TH ULTIMATE-REMOTE 1 "October 2026" "Ultimate Remote @APP_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ultimate-remote \- infrared remote control for Cardputer Zero
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ultimate-remote
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uses the Linux framebuffer, evdev keyboard and kernel LIRC transmitter.
The default IR TX pin is GPIO12; the kernel overlay must select the same pin.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --ir-tx-pin " GPIO"
Set the expected transmitter GPIO. Does not reconfigure the kernel overlay.
.TP
.BI --lirc-device " PATH"
Select the LIRC transmitter (default /dev/lirc0).
.TP
.BI --input-device " PATH"
Use only the specified evdev keyboard.
.TP
.B --input-debug
Log keyboard events.
.TP
.B --ir-test
Send a test NEC frame and exit.
.TP
.B --help
Print command-line usage.
.TP
.B --version
Print the application version and exit.
.SH CONTROLS
F/X: up/down. Z/C: left/right in the home carousel. Enter: select.
Esc: back one screen per press. Space: manage favorites.
Z also goes back in the Online IR browser. Tab no longer goes back.
On the home carousel, hold Esc for three seconds to exit to APPLaunch.
The message "Hold 3sec to return to home" and a progress bar appear while held.
Releasing early cancels. A press started in a submenu cannot exit the app;
release and press Esc again on the home carousel.
In search fields, hold Fn to type a navigation letter (F/X, and Z in Online IR).
Favorite names accept letters directly. Backspace deletes.
The built-in tca8418c keyboard reports KEY_DVD and translated media/arrow keys;
the app decodes this layer into Fn letters. Generic KEY_FN events are also supported.
The built-in keyboard is grabbed while the app runs to prevent duplicate
console input and system media actions; exiting releases it.
In a terminal, use Alt+letter instead; ANSI arrow keys also navigate.
The hold gesture requires evdev key-release events. With terminal input only,
Esc goes back and Ctrl+C exits.
.SS Remote command shortcuts
In built-in and Online IR command lists: Fn+S is volume down, Fn+A mute,
Fn+D volume up, Fn+Q play, Fn+W rewind and Fn+E forward.
Previous/Next are used if Rewind/Forward are absent; Play/Pause is used if Play
is absent. Each command's badge shows its assigned shortcut.
Fn+F/X/C/Z sends remote Up/Down/Right/Left. Without Fn, F/X still navigate and
Z goes back. Each modified command requires a fresh letter press.
Outside command lists, Fn retains its text/filter behavior. Terminal users
can use Alt+letter for the same command shortcuts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/ultimate-remote
System defaults (shell assignments).
.TP
.I ~/.config/ultimate-remote/config
Optional per-user configuration. Respects XDG_CONFIG_HOME.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ultimate-remote/favoriteRemotes.txt
User favorites. Respects XDG_STATE_HOME or ULTIMATE_REMOTE_STATE_DIR.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/ultimate-remote/flipper-irdb/
Catalog and downloaded IR remotes. Respects XDG_CACHE_HOME or ULTIMATE_REMOTE_IRDB_CACHE.
.SH IR DATABASE
Browse the public Lucaslhm/Flipper-IRDB GitHub repository by category, brand and
model. Selected remotes are downloaded and cached for offline use.
Select Refresh catalog at the catalog root to update. Back cancels downloads.
Requires Python 3, CA certificates and a network connection for uncached data.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I /usr/share/doc/ultimate-remote/README.md
